WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.150
- I have always been
attracted to visionaries,

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.900
comedians and people who make me laugh.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.980
I was so attracted to our next guest.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.417
I even married him.

00:00:10.417 --> 00:00:11.424
Yeah, (laughing)

00:00:11.424 --> 00:00:12.257
(audience laughing)

00:00:12.257 --> 00:00:13.870
'cause that's what you do.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.720
Please welcome.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.330
A wonderful, wonderful man,

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:18.518
Tom green.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:21.467
(audience applauding)

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:22.940
- Hi Drew. (laughs)

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.280
Hi everybody. (laughs)

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.480
I brought Charlie with me.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.850
Hello Drew, how are you?

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:29.140
- I'm--
- Nice to see you.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.250
- I'm so good.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.885
I know you have a new woman in your life.

00:00:32.885 --> 00:00:33.820
(laughs)

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.720
- Yes. This is my new puppy, Charlie

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.260
and we were taken off on a van trip

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.410
and we're gonna travel
around the country together

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.060
and I'm really looking forward to it,

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.520
but great to see you

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.770
and congratulations on
your incredible show.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.720
I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.300
And was so happy when you
invited me on the show.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.133
Thank you so much.

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.260
This is amazing.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:57.880
- I am little backstory for anyone

00:00:59.208 --> 00:01:02.170
is that we haven't seen
or spoken to each other

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.150
in far too long.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:05.150
- Thanks for having me here Drew

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:06.700
and I'm really, really

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.260
couldn't be more excited
about your new show.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.150
It's nice to see you every day on here.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.080
Just bringing this burst of happiness

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.450
and energy

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:15.590
and optimism

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.040
to the world right now.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.127
(audience applauding)

00:01:18.127 --> 00:01:19.170
- Thank you.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:20.100
- Dick and Mary Jane,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.210
my mother and father,
they say hello by the way.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.290
And they're really happy
that I'm here on the show

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:26.580
and they're happy for you.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.064
And we're all really
happy for you actually.

00:01:29.064 --> 00:01:31.940
We love watching you do amazing things

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.080
and we're so excited about your new show.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:37.340
- I've had two nights of
great sleep in my life

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.770
before my daughters were born.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:41.710
And I don't know why but sleep is like,

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.760
it's just been like a weird thing for me.

00:01:45.351 --> 00:01:47.700
And I remember this night
just being so content

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.753
and I was at your parents' lake house.

00:01:50.869 --> 00:01:53.200
And I remember hearing
all their voices upstairs

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.450
and I was just by myself
and I was going to sleep

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.780
And I was like, "yeah,
this is what you know

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.800
safety and contentedness feels

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:01.010
before you're going to sleep."

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.160
And I will never forget that night.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.500
And I love your parents
and I really love you.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.345
And I celebrate you.

00:02:07.345 --> 00:02:09.410
And you know, when you say like, 20 years

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.763
it's sometimes it's a blink of an eye.

00:02:11.763 --> 00:02:12.596
(laughs tearfully)

00:02:12.596 --> 00:02:13.527
And sometimes you're like,

00:02:13.527 --> 00:02:17.320
"Oh my God, we've lived so
much in these last 20 years."

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:18.730
You've had a whole life

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.510
and I've had a whole life

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.700
and it's just really nice to come together

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.490
and check in and talk about it.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:27.700
It just, it thrills me to no end.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:29.230
And I think the world of you

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:32.577
and I celebrate you and I
always have and I always will.

00:02:32.577 --> 00:02:34.261
- Thank you Drew, thank you.

00:02:34.261 --> 00:02:35.160
(audience applauding)

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.280
- This is a really...

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.380
I was so happy when you
invited me on the show.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:40.213
It's been too long.

00:02:40.213 --> 00:02:41.490
We should have, you know,

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:43.160
it's nice to reconnect.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:46.680
We really did not talk for
about 15 years, I guess.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.770
And this is really the
first time we've looked

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.803
at each other face to face in 15 years.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.780
- One of the things that means so much

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.430
to me professionally also

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:00.590
is because one of the reasons
that we got to know each other

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:01.430
in the first place

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:04.820
was I admired your work so much.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:07.320
And so I reached out to you

00:03:08.496 --> 00:03:10.690
and asked you to come
and do Charlie's Angels.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.907
And you so graciously said, "yes."

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:15.710
But that was so exciting

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.460
getting to do that movie with you.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:22.310
And you know we kind of,
sort of hit it off right away

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:23.510
pretty much.
- Yeah.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:25.600
- We had a lot of laughs together.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.360
I think one of our first dates

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.530
I think we went bought lobsters,

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:32.410
'cause we both love animals

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:34.820
and we both got lobsters

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.770
and we released them

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.307
into the ocean.

00:03:39.307 --> 00:03:40.670
That was what we decided to do.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:41.503
- We did.

00:03:41.503 --> 00:03:43.690
And you brought me a camera

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.870
and I still have it,

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.530
the Pentax K1000.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:50.370
And you got me started
into what would become

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:55.247
you know, two decades full
of being a real photographer.

00:03:56.626 --> 00:03:59.220
And you got me into my
whole Annie Hall phase

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:02.530
of taking photographs,

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:03.990
which is such a beautiful art.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:07.620
And it tracks me back
to what you were doing

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:08.453
when you did it.

00:04:08.453 --> 00:04:10.990
There was no technology available.

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:12.230
There was no internet.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:15.100
There was like no cell phones.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.590
There was no social media.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:21.540
And you opened the
floodgates of all of it.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.080
And you did it in this way

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:26.840
where you really messed with people,

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.510
but it wasn't mean, and it wasn't angry.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:31.390
And when you can go that far

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.430
and push the envelope

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.720
to that degree--

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.430
- What'd you say about not being mean?

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:38.910
That that was always part of it.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:40.470
I would never wanna do
something to someone

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:41.520
that was actually mean.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.530
But if I went out and did
something really stupid

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.950
and they got mad at me,

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.650
that was the humor in it for me.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:50.290
- I mean, did you start with a camcorder?

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.200
- I like tech, you know I'm a geek, right?

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.193
- Yes. (laughing)

00:04:53.193 --> 00:04:54.356
- I like technology.

00:04:54.356 --> 00:04:55.189
(laughing)

00:04:55.189 --> 00:04:56.890
I like technology

00:04:56.890 --> 00:05:01.320
and I like cameras and
computers and editing.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.410
And I'm always playing
with the latest technology.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:07.400
So, sometimes when you
see what the new camera is

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.550
or the new microphone

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:11.340
or the new editing
machine that's coming out,

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:12.590
you try to think how you're gonna do

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:13.720
something creative with that.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:16.020
And then we just went out
and made this crazy show

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.790
and we were in our early 20s

00:05:19.682 --> 00:05:21.890
and just were wild and ridiculous

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:23.340
and had a great time.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:26.010
And I remember when MTV picked up the show

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:28.400
and moved me down to New York city,

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:29.980
how exciting it was.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:32.650
And I remember you
called over to the studio

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.617
and that was very cool, very exciting.

00:05:35.617 --> 00:05:36.530
(Drew laughs)

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:38.990
And then eventually when
I moved to Los Angeles,

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:40.580
I met you and we did Charlie's Angels.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:43.190
And now travels with Charlie.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.700
Maybe it makes sense

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:47.140
that The Chad would have a
dog named Charlie, right?

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:47.993
I'm The Chad.

00:05:47.993 --> 00:05:48.826
- Yeees. (clapping and laughing)

00:05:48.826 --> 00:05:49.659
(audience applauding)

00:05:49.659 --> 00:05:51.950
You're The Chad.
- I'm The Chad.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.140
I'm The Chad.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:54.468
- It might be The Chad.

00:05:54.468 --> 00:05:55.301
- I'm The Chad.

00:05:55.301 --> 00:05:56.925
Good morning Starfish.

00:05:56.925 --> 00:05:58.125
- Good morning The Chad.

00:05:59.427 --> 00:06:00.629
(laughing)

00:06:00.629 --> 00:06:03.212
(upbeat music)

